::meta{crate: tomet-sort, dependencies: list(), dependents: list()}

=[tomet-sort]

==[Overview & Scope]

Pure character and dictionary collation, sort keys, and ordering primitives.

==[Architecture & Responsibilities]

- ("Pure base crate") This crate is in the base layer (`crates/tomet-base-*`) and depends on
nothing in the workspace. It contains zero unsafe code and no external
dependencies.
- ("Two-level collation") Equivalence groups share a primary weight and are distinguished by
secondary weights. Streaming comparison compares primary weights first,
enforces prefix dominance, and breaks ties with secondary weights.
- ("Greedy longest match") Multi-character tokens are matched greedily using an internal UTF-8 trie,
falling back to Unicode scalar values for unmapped characters.

==[Module collator]

Compiled collation engine and zero-allocation comparison iterators.

===[Structs]

====[struct Collator]

A compiled collator for comparing and sorting strings according to custom collation rules.

==[Module direction]

Directional collation modes and ordering transformations.

===[Enums]

====[enum Direction]

The ordering direction for collation comparisons.

==[Module error]

Validation and compilation errors for collation specifications.

===[Enums]

====[enum CollationError]

An error encountered when validating or compiling a collation specification.

==[Module key]

Opaque collation keys for two-level lexicographical ordering.

===[Structs]

====[struct SortKey]

A 2-level collation key used for comparing strings.

Collation keys are compared lexicographically by primary weights first.
If and only if both strings produce identical primary weight sequences,
ties are broken by secondary weights.

==[Module spec]

Declarative specification of collation steps, equivalence groups, and ignored tokens.

===[Structs]

====[struct CollationSpec]

A declarative specification for custom character and string collation.

===[Enums]

====[enum Step]

A single step in a collation sequence.
